Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 23:21:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 183/209] refactor(area): pairwise shape incompatibility helper

"Exactly one shape component per entity" (decision 01) is enforced by every
shape kind declaring every other kind incompatible. The check is
one-directional - EntityObject.cpp:729 walks the components already on the
entity and asks each of them IsCompatibleWith(candidate) - so each pair has to
be declared on both sides: n*(n-1) declarations, 12 for the four kinds of the
first wave. Written by hand in each ReflectType, that list rots the first time
a kind is added and one direction is forgotten.

Module/Shapes/ShapeKinds.h now holds the single list of kinds and their
component GUIDs as an X-macro, plus DeclareShapeKindIncompatibilities(desc),
which declares the calling kind incompatible with every other entry. Adding a
kind is one line in AREA_SHAPE_COMPONENT_LIST.

- The Spline slot is declared before the kind exists. An Incompatibility naming
  a GUID nothing has registered is inert, because IsCompatibleWith only ever
  compares it against components actually present, so the slot costs nothing.
- The GUIDs stay spelled out rather than pulled from the kind headers: every
  kind would otherwise have to include every other kind's header, which is a
  cycle. ShapeKinds.h includes none of them and each kind includes only it.
- ShapeComponentGuid::Box() ... Sphere() come out of the same list, for the
  places that need to name one specific kind.

Box and Polygon replace their hand-written single declaration with the call;
behaviour is identical, and both now also declare the Sphere and Spline slots.

